## Part 1 — CSS

### 1. Universal Selector + Reset
```css
* {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

- `*` targets every element
- Removes default browser margin and padding
- `box-sizing: border-box` keeps padding and border inside the width

### 2. Body Styling
```css
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.6;
  background-color: #f4f4f4;
  color: #333;
}
```

- Sets default font for the whole page
- `line-height: 1.6` makes text easier to read
- Light gray background and dark text

### 3. Header + Flexbox
```css
header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}
```

- `display: flex` makes the header a flexible container
- `justify-content: space-between` pushes name to the left and links to the right
- `align-items: center` vertically centers items

This is the most important concept today.

### 4. Navigation Links
```css
nav a {
  color: white;
  text-decoration: none;
  margin-left: 20px;
}

nav a:hover {
  color: #00bcd4;
}
```

- Removes underline from links
- Adds space between links
- `:hover` changes color when the mouse is over the link

### 5. Main Content Centering
```css
main {
  max-width: 900px;
  margin: 40px auto;
}
```

- Limits width so it doesn’t stretch too wide on big screens
- `margin: 40px auto` centers the content horizontally

### 6. Section Cards
```css
section {
  background: white;
  padding: 30px;
  margin-bottom: 30px;
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```

- White background creates a card effect
- Padding = space inside
- Margin = space outside
- Border-radius = rounded corners

### 7. Footer
Simple centered text with a dark background.

### Core CSS Ideas
- Margin = space outside the element
- Padding = space inside the element
- Flexbox = best way to align items in a row
- Hover = interactive state

